    "body": "Fixes Issue: #1009 which reports a variety of issues related to P2PK and HTLC and SIG_ALL. Even if some of those features have been partially implemented and tested together, problems arise when they are combined; for example, a post-locktime HTLC with SIG_ALL\r\n\r\n_Starting with the mint:_\r\n\r\nEven if we update Nutshell to use the new SIG_ALL message format (https://github.com/cashubtc/nuts/pull/302), it still has the incorrect behaviour on a variety of scenarios involving P2PK and HTLC. See the Issue above for more.\r\n\r\nThe existing code had NUT-10 code in multiple places. In this PR, following the CDK architecture, all the NUT-10 logic is moved into a single boolean function `_verify_transaction_spending_conditions`. This unifies checking for swap and melt and minimizes code duplication.\r\n\r\nThat new function first checks if any proof has SIG_ALL. If yes, a SIG_ALL validation is performed; otherwise, a different path is taken to check the proofs individually for compatibility with all the P2PK and HTLC rules.\r\n\r\nThis PR uses the same `SpendingRequirements` class as used in the CDK, to unify the requirements\r\n\r\n_Wallet:_ The only wallet change here is to keep up with the new SIG_ALL message format.",
